  "$comment": "p15-oracle-063: the session family's 11 mutations (gen_daemon_ops.py reads this file; run it after an edit). Each success case makes the fixture workspace, runs the operation, reads the durable lists (workspaces, panes, tabs and the journal lists the operation changes), restarts the daemon gracefully on the same state root (restart: shutdown-daemon that keeps the terminals, then a start that adopts them; session.shutdown is that stop itself), waits for the terminal to run again, reads the same lists, which must equal the replies before, and gets the fixture workspace, pane, tab and terminal by their ids from before the restart. The restart step's before and settled snapshots let I2 hold every structural id. Error cases stay the catalog-type refusal on a fresh daemon.",
